  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Us Foods holds $216M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date and received 77 awards this fiscal year. Us Foods average award size is $2.8M. Us Foods obligations are down 15.3% year over year. Us Foods sales to federal buyers concentrate in food manufacturing and food service NAICS categories: All Other Miscellaneous Food Manufacturing shows $216M, Perishable Prepared Food Manufacturing shows $276K, and Food Service Contractors shows $10.9K. Us Foods has a clear agency concentration: the Department of Veterans Affairs accounts for $170M of FY2026 obligations, the Department of Defense accounts for $32.8M, and the Department of Agriculture accounts for $7.5M. Us Foods also has FY2026 obligations with the Department of the Interior at $3.3M, the Department of the Treasury at $1.4M, and the Department of Health and Human Services at $1.3M. Historical obligations moved from $143M in FY21 to $255M in FY25, then to $216M in FY26.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2026 performance compare with prior years?",
        "body": "Us Foods obligated $216M in FY2026 to date. Us Foods obligations rose from $143M in FY21 to $255M in FY25, then fell to $216M in FY26. Us Foods obligations are down 15.3% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are the biggest buyers of Us Foods this year?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the largest buyer, obligating $170M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $32.8M and the Department of Agriculture obligated $7.5M. The Department of the Interior, the Department of the Treasury, and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $3.3M, $1.4M, and $1.3M respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
